-- חוק דמי מחלה (היעדרות בשל מחלת ילד), התשנ"ג-1993 — sections 1, 1א, 1ב,
-- 1ג, 3 and 3א: the days an employee may charge to his accrued sick leave
-- for the illness of a child under 16 (8, or 16 with the child in his sole
-- custody or as its single parent), for a serious illness of a child under
-- 18 (90, or 110), and to give personal assistance to his child with a
-- disability (18 days and 18 more, and 52 hours and 52 more without loss of
-- pay); a foster parent's share in them; that the law adds to every other
-- right; and that the State is an employer like any other. The text is
-- laws/sick-pay-child-law.toml, pinned from the live page of ספר החוקים
-- הפתוח; the corpus holds no copy (MMS-601).
--
-- Why it is here: the takanon's §1.25.3.1 restates §§1 to 1ג as its
-- clauses 3 to 3ג and lists the law among its sources. Where a restatement
-- gives less, the law governs (§3 here; the root's precedence,
-- l4/lib/precedence.l4; convention instruments.statute-floor). Unlike the
-- Sick Pay Law's §§2 to 6, this law reaches an employee whatever
-- collective agreement regulates his sick pay: its "employee" is not
-- narrowed, and §3 says it adds to every right by law or agreement.

IMPORT prelude

@desc An employee's family, as the Child Illness Law asks about it.
DECLARE `a parent's family under the Child Illness Law` HAS
    `the spouse is an employee and did not take the absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc "בן זוגו הוא עובד ולא נעדר מעבודתו מכוח זכאותו כאמור"
    `the spouse is self-employed and did not leave the business for it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee is the child's single parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc "הורה עצמאי", as the Single-Parent Families Law 1992 defines it
    `the child is in the employee's sole custody` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months with the employer` IS A NUMBER @desc for the same employer or at the same workplace

-- The families the checks below ask about.
`a single parent of a year's service` MEANS
    `a parent's family under the Child Illness Law` WITH
        `the spouse is an employee and did not take the absence` IS FALSE
        `the spouse is self-employed and did not leave the business for it` IS FALSE
        `the employee is the child's single parent` IS TRUE
        `the child is in the employee's sole custody` IS FALSE
        `months with the employer` IS 12

`a parent whose spouse works, of a year's service` MEANS
    `a parent's family under the Child Illness Law` WITH
        `the spouse is an employee and did not take the absence` IS TRUE
        `the spouse is self-employed and did not leave the business for it` IS FALSE
        `the employee is the child's single parent` IS FALSE
        `the child is in the employee's sole custody` IS FALSE
        `months with the employer` IS 12

`a parent whose spouse does not work, of a year's service` MEANS
    `a parent's family under the Child Illness Law` WITH
        `the spouse is an employee and did not take the absence` IS FALSE
        `the spouse is self-employed and did not leave the business for it` IS FALSE
        `the employee is the child's single parent` IS FALSE
        `the child is in the employee's sole custody` IS FALSE
        `months with the employer` IS 12

§ `חוק דמי מחלה (היעדרות בשל מחלת ילד) — הימים שהעובד זוקף`

§§ `1`

-- An employee with a child under 16 may charge to his accrued sick leave,
-- for the child's illness, (א) up to 8 days a year where his spouse is an
-- employee who did not take the absence, or self-employed and did not
-- leave the business on those days; (ב) up to 16 where the child is in his
-- sole custody or he is its single parent. None where neither holds.
@ref law:1
GIVEN `age of the child` IS A NUMBER, f IS A `a parent's family under the Child Illness Law`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days a year section 1 of the Child Illness Law gives` `age of the child` f IS
    IF `age of the child` AT LEAST 16
    THEN 0
    ELSE BRANCH IF f's `the child is in the employee's sole custody` OR f's `the employee is the child's single parent` THEN 16
                IF f's `the spouse is an employee and did not take the absence`
                   OR f's `the spouse is self-employed and did not leave the business for it` THEN 8
                OTHERWISE 0

#ASSERT `days a year section 1 of the Child Illness Law gives` 5 `a parent whose spouse works, of a year's service` EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `days a year section 1 of the Child Illness Law gives` 5 `a single parent of a year's service` EQUALS 16
#ASSERT `days a year section 1 of the Child Illness Law gives` 16 `a single parent of a year's service` EQUALS 0

§§ `1א`

-- (א): an employee with a child under 18, after a year with the employer
-- or at the workplace, may charge up to 90 days a year for a serious
-- illness of the child, to his accrued sick leave or his vacation, as he
-- chooses; up to 110 where his spouse is an employee who did not take the
-- absence, or he is a single parent, or the child is in his sole custody.
-- (ב): the days charged under §1 count. (ג): a serious illness is a
-- malignant one, one that needs regular dialysis, or another the Minister
-- sets by order.
@desc A child's illness, as section 1א(ג) tells a serious one.
DECLARE `a child's illness under section 1א` IS ONE OF
    `a malignant illness of the child`
    `an illness of the child that needs regular dialysis`
    `another illness of the child the Minister set by order`
    `an illness of the child that is none of these`

@ref law:1א
GIVEN i IS A `a child's illness under section 1א`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a serious illness as section 1א means` i IF
    NOT i EQUALS `an illness of the child that is none of these`

@ref law:1א
GIVEN `age of the child` IS A NUMBER
      i IS A `a child's illness under section 1א`
      f IS A `a parent's family under the Child Illness Law`
      `days already charged under section 1` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days left a year under section 1א of the Child Illness Law` `age of the child` i f `days already charged under section 1` IS
    IF `age of the child` AT LEAST 18
       OR f's `months with the employer` LESS THAN 12
       OR NOT `a serious illness as section 1א means` i
    THEN 0
    ELSE max 0 (`ceiling` MINUS `days already charged under section 1`)
    WHERE
        `ceiling` MEANS
            IF     f's `the spouse is an employee and did not take the absence`
                OR f's `the employee is the child's single parent`
                OR f's `the child is in the employee's sole custody`
            THEN 110
            ELSE 90

@ref law:1א
`section 1א lets the employee charge a serious illness's days to his vacation instead, as he chooses` MEANS TRUE

#ASSERT `days left a year under section 1א of the Child Illness Law` 10 `an illness of the child that needs regular dialysis` `a parent whose spouse does not work, of a year's service` 0 EQUALS 90
#ASSERT `days left a year under section 1א of the Child Illness Law` 10 `a malignant illness of the child` `a single parent of a year's service` 6 EQUALS 104
#ASSERT `days left a year under section 1א of the Child Illness Law` 10 `an illness of the child that is none of these` `a single parent of a year's service` 0 EQUALS 0

§§ `1ב`

-- (א): a parent of a person with a disability, after a year with the
-- employer or at the workplace, may charge up to 18 days a year, to his
-- accrued sick leave or his vacation as he chooses, to give the personal
-- assistance the person needs; and up to 18 more where (1) his spouse is an
-- employee who did not take it, (2) his spouse is self-employed and did not
-- leave the business for it, (3) he is a single parent, or (4) the person
-- is in his sole custody — provided no other person used the additional
-- days for the same person. (א1): parts of days count, and sick pay is due
-- from the first day. (א2): besides, up to 52 hours a year of absence for
-- that assistance without loss of pay, and 52 more on (1)–(4), in
-- proportion for a part-time position (its share against a full one or 186
-- hours a month, the lower). (ב): a guardian likewise, where no other cares
-- for the person and no other guardian used it. (ג): days under §§1 and 1א
-- for the same child count. (ה): not for a disability that is not
-- permanent and should pass within 60 days and not recur.
@ref law:1ב
GIVEN f IS A `a parent's family under the Child Illness Law`
      `another person used the additional days for the same person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 1ב opens the additional days` f `another person used the additional days for the same person` IF
        (   f's `the spouse is an employee and did not take the absence`
         OR f's `the spouse is self-employed and did not leave the business for it`
         OR f's `the employee is the child's single parent`
         OR f's `the child is in the employee's sole custody`)
    AND NOT `another person used the additional days for the same person`

@ref law:1ב
`additional days a year section 1ב(א) gives` MEANS 18

@ref law:1ב
GIVEN f IS A `a parent's family under the Child Illness Law`
      `another person used the additional days for the same person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days already charged under sections 1 and 1א for the same child` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days left a year under section 1ב of the Child Illness Law` f `another person used the additional days for the same person` `days already charged under sections 1 and 1א for the same child` IS
    IF f's `months with the employer` LESS THAN 12
    THEN 0
    ELSE max 0 (`ceiling` MINUS `days already charged under sections 1 and 1א for the same child`)
    WHERE
        `ceiling` MEANS
            18 PLUS (IF `section 1ב opens the additional days` f `another person used the additional days for the same person`
                     THEN `additional days a year section 1ב(א) gives`
                     ELSE 0)

@ref law:1ב
GIVEN f IS A `a parent's family under the Child Illness Law`
      `another person used the additional hours for the same person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `his monthly working hours` IS A NUMBER @desc the average of his fullest quarter in the 12 months before
      `a full position's monthly hours at his workplace` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `paid hours a year section 1ב(א2) gives` f `another person used the additional hours for the same person` `his monthly working hours` `a full position's monthly hours at his workplace` IS
    `the hours of a full position` TIMES `his share of a position`
    WHERE
        `the hours of a full position` MEANS
            52 PLUS (IF `section 1ב opens the additional days` f `another person used the additional hours for the same person`
                     THEN 52
                     ELSE 0)
        `his share of a position` MEANS
            min 1 (`his monthly working hours` DIVIDED BY (min `a full position's monthly hours at his workplace` 186))

#ASSERT `days left a year under section 1ב of the Child Illness Law` `a parent whose spouse works, of a year's service` FALSE 0 EQUALS 36
#ASSERT `days left a year under section 1ב of the Child Illness Law` `a parent whose spouse does not work, of a year's service` FALSE 0 EQUALS 18
#ASSERT `paid hours a year section 1ב(א2) gives` `a parent whose spouse works, of a year's service` FALSE 93 186 EQUALS 52

§§ `1ג`

-- §§1 to 1ב apply to a foster parent, but his days are charged only where
-- the natural or adoptive parent did not use the same right on those days.
@ref law:1ג
GIVEN `the natural or adoptive parent used the right on those days` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 1ג charges a foster parent's days` `the natural or adoptive parent used the right on those days` IF
    NOT `the natural or adoptive parent used the right on those days`

#ASSERT `section 1ג charges a foster parent's days` FALSE

§§ `3`

-- The law adds to an employee's right by law or agreement and takes none
-- away: for a right measured in one number, the larger stands.
@ref law:3
GIVEN `what the law gives` IS A NUMBER, `what the instrument gives` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what stands under section 3 of the Child Illness Law` `what the law gives` `what the instrument gives` IS
    max `what the law gives` `what the instrument gives`

#ASSERT `what stands under section 3 of the Child Illness Law` 18 15 EQUALS 18

§§ `3א`

-- For this law the State as employer is like any other employer.
@ref law:3א
`the Child Illness Law binds the State as an employer` MEANS TRUE
